  "title": "Group Shifted Strings",
  "summary": "Given an array of strings, group all strings that belong to the same shifting sequence.",
  "statement": "Given an array of strings, group all strings that belong to the same shifting sequence. A shifting sequence is formed by repeatedly applying right or left shifts to a string. For example, \"abc\" and \"bcd\" are part of the same shifting sequence. Return the grouped strings in any order.",
  "constraints": [
    "strings contains 1–200 lowercase strings, each of length 1–50; duplicate strings are retained as separate input occurrences.",
    "Group strings that differ by adding the same alphabetic shift modulo 26 to every position. Group order and order within each group do not matter."
  ],
  "topics": [
    "strings",
    "hash-maps",
    "modular-arithmetic"
  ],
